  51 prompt files in 19 folders, 716,315 bytes (727,644 with its README)
  head ee999ee66d31828a39fe155a52ce66d42db7bf18, 11 November 2026
  read 12 November 2026
  16,208 stars at the time of reading

The collection carries NO licence file: no LICENSE, no terms in the README beyond
a "research and educational purposes only" warning. So this cell redistributes
none of it. DATA.LISP holds each file's path, size, line count and sha256, all
measured; a prompt is fetched from the author's own repository when a reader asks
for it, cached in that reader's home, and quoted with its file and line. If a
quotation is a problem, the file name and the line number say which one to point
at.

What is ours: the reading - which model each file targets, what kind of file it
is, which files are byte-identical to each other, and the one-line description
of each. Where our reading and a file disagree, the file wins: quote it.

No prompt is reproduced in DATA.LISP. Nothing here is a claim that any prompt
works on any model it was not written for.
